AB  - Uncontrolled cell growth in the brain, known as a tumour, can lead to symptoms like constant headaches, nausea, and seizures. Magnetic resonance imaging -MRI-is the main standard for detecting brain tumours, while computed tomography (CT) serves as a viable alternative. Early diagnosis is crucial for improving treatment outcomes. Therefore, an automated diagnostic approach that reduces diagnostic time while enhancing accuracy is urgently needed. This paper proposes a novel mobile augmented reality (AR) application designed to support brain tumour diagnosis. The application integrates intuitive gesture-based interaction with a 3D U-Net-powered segmentation model to deliver real-time, interactive 3D visualisations of tumours. Clinicians can dynamically manipulate views, zoom into regions of interest, and toggle between MRI fusion layers, enabling flexible application across diagnostic workflows, surgical planning, and patient education. Preliminary trials demonstrate the application’s effectiveness in increasing diagnostic confidence and reducing interpretation time. Initial feedback from medical professionals has been positive, particularly highlighting its user-centric design and clinical adaptability.
ER  - 

