AB  - Virtual reality (VR) is increasingly adopted for simulation-based training, yet head-mounted displays (HMDs) often occlude upper facial regions, reducing the reliability of facial expression recognition (FER). This paper introduces a facial expression-aware VR training pipeline that integrates exemplar-guided facial inpainting (EXE-GAN) to reconstruct occluded regions prior to emotion detection using the Google Vision API. A paired evaluation with N = 17 participants compared the emotion recognition performance without and with EXE-GAN preprocessing. Nonparametric analysis (Wilcoxon signed rank test) revealed a significant improvement in the Happy score (mean ∆=+ 0.312, W =0.0, p=0.0277), with a small to moderate effect size (Cliff δ=0.353). A complementary metric, the Happy Dominance Ratio Happy/(Happy+Neutral), also increased significantly (mean ∆=+0.0269, W =2.0, p=0.0425; Cliff’s δ=0.294). Other emotion categories showed minimal or no change. These findings suggest that exemplar-guided reconstruction enhances FER robustness for positive affect under HMD occlusion, offering a practical and portable solution for emotion-aware VR simulation training.
ER  - 

