AB  - Task guidance is key to skill acquisition in areas like manufacturing and cooking. While traditional tools (e.g., laptops, paper) offer support, augmented reality (AR) enables immersive, context-aware assistance. We present a task guidance framework for Apple Vision Pro, integrating voice input, large language models, and object detection for real-time, user-tailored instructions. A user study (N=18) compared our AR system with a PDF recipe and a laptop-based app during a smoothie-making task. Results show that while AR enhanced engagement, the task’s simplicity favored the laptop in performance.
