AB  - This paper investigates the scenario-based development of intangible cultural heritage (ICH) ceramic art under the background of digital intelligence. To address the limitations of traditional qualitative cultural studies, this research proposes a quantitative, technology-driven framework for ICH ceramic preservation and industrialization. By integrating 3D scanning, Artificial Intelligence (AI) generative design, and Virtual Reality/Augmented Reality (VR/AR) interaction, a digital platform architecture for ICH ceramics is constructed. An empirical study involving 135 participants was conducted to evaluate the system's effectiveness across six dimensions. The experimental results demonstrate that the digital intelligence intervention significantly improved user experience scores by 31.4% and market recognition by $\mathbf{1 3. 9 \%}$ compared to traditional methods. Furthermore, the AI-assisted design module reduced the average product prototyping cycle by 68.4%, from 72.1 hours to 22.8 hours. The findings provide solid engineering evidence that the deep integration of digital technologies and ICH ceramics offers an effective path for sustainable protection, creative transformation, and industrial upgrading.
