AB  - Traditional museum tours rely on paper maps and tour guides, which are not intuitive and difficult to meet personalized needs. This paper proposes a set of technical solutions based on computer-aided design (CAD) to solve the design problems of immersive environments in digital museums. This paper digitally models the exhibits and exhibition spaces of the museum to generate high-precision three-dimensional models. Using Unity3D, combined with VR (virtual reality) and AR (augmented reality) technologies, immersive exhibition scenes and interactive processes are designed. Then, visual, auditory and tactile feedback is combined to further enhance the audience's sense of immersion. Compared with traditional guided tours, the average stay time of the audience in the immersive environment is significantly extended, the frequency of interactive operations is increased, and the scores in multiple evaluation dimensions such as learnability and efficiency are higher. This method provides new ideas for the development of digital museums.
