AB  - We present PM4Panorama, a scriptable parametric modeling interface for designing interactive 360° panorama videos from static panoramic images using text-image-to-video generation in virtual reality (VR). Built on PM4VR, a programmable parametric modeling framework for immersive environments, PM4Panorama enables users to define prompts, camera viewpoints, and spatial transformations directly through scripts, while seamlessly integrating modern text-image-to-video diffusion models. Our system introduces an end-to-end workflow that transforms a single panoramic image into a dynamic 360° panoramic video content through view sampling, prompt-conditioned video synthesis, and parametric surface mapping in VR. PM4Panorama allows users to not only experience generated panorama videos immersively but also to procedurally control and redesign parametric shapes in real time. We demonstrate how scriptable interaction, parametric geometry, and generative AI models can be unified into a coherent system for controllable and extensible panorama 360° video creation.
ER  - 

